---
/**
 * ACADEMIC PHILOSOPHY · EXPERIENTIAL & INQUIRY-BASED LEARNING — audit §2A.
 *
 * ⚠ FOUR SECTIONS AND A CLOSE, not the movement-plus-notes pattern this page
 * used to carry. It previously rendered PhilosophyStory's `hands` movement with
 * TopicNotes under it, which was right while the six sub-topics shared one
 * composed sequence; the client has since asked for a short, art-directed page
 * instead. Nothing was removed from /academics/philosophy/ — the overview still
 * carries its own `hands`.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero, DELIBERATELY. The brief asks for an
 * immersive hero rather than a banner, but the client's standing instruction on
 * this project — given after a bespoke hero was built and rejected on the
 * Student-Centred page — is that the banner stays consistent with every other
 * page. That instruction wins. The art direction the brief asks for lives in the
 * four sections below it, where it can be different without the masthead area
 * behaving unlike the rest of the site.
 *
 * ⚠ SOURCES AND THE TWO CLAIMS NOT MADE are documented at the top of
 * ExperientialPage: Chandrayaan-3 and a "Science & Mathematics Exhibition" are
 * offered by the brief as examples but appear neither on the school's site nor
 * in this repository, so neither is on the page.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import ExperientialPage from '../../../components/academics/ExperientialPage.astro';
import banner from '../../../assets/chem lab/DSC_1262 copy.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={banner}
  />

  {/* padding-block: 0 — every section carries its own rhythm, and the panel
      adding its own on top is what put a 183px void under the hero on three
      earlier pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel ex-panel">
    <ExperientialPage />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ex-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
